Falsifies `capability::the_peak_never_falls_and_a_floor_insert_stays_above_its_floor`.

The defect: `first_free_from` shifts its mask the wrong way, so the lowest free slot "at or above
the floor" is the lowest free slot below the end of the floor's complement, and a floor insert can
land under its floor.

Expected to fail: `assert!(slot >= floor, "a floor insert landed below its floor")`, on any table
with a free slot below a nonzero floor.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index a5b8f24b3..af7d3fd74 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@ mod storage {
             let above = if floor >= 64 {
                 0
             } else {
-                self.free & (u64::MAX << floor)
+                self.free & (u64::MAX >> floor)
             };
             (above != 0).then(|| above.trailing_zeros() as usize)
         }
